Bugfix: Make the file row actions buttons instead of nested links

The share and menu actions of every file row were anchors without a target,
placed inside the link that opens the file. Screen readers announced three
links per row where there is one file, and two of them led nowhere.

Both actions are buttons now, and they sit beside the file link rather than
inside it. Each row offers one link to its file and two buttons next to it,
and the appearance is unchanged.

WCAG 2.1 AA, SC 2.4.4
